# Level 4's own objects as the original runs them: levels 1 to 3 won at
# their 20th frame ($A07 and $A6C set), so the game loads level 4 as it
# would; the ship kept alive, still and firing, the shop skipped (as
# level-run.exp). Once the world is held by the mid boss the ship is put
# under its pods and its chain (x 120 at frame 2700, 200 at 3300, 160 at
# 3900); at 5200 the world let go ($CE8 cleared); at the end boss, under
# its claws and its head (x 128 at 7700, 192 at 8100, 160 at 8500). Logged
# every frame ($3E42): the frame, the world line, fire, the ship and its
# box, the step, the back limit and the random generator; every enemy
# destroyed ($6250) and token taken ($4FF8); every update of an object of
# the level's own code as it starts (21 routines): its pc, object, type,
# x, y, +40, +48 and hit points. For porting level 4's own code frame by
# frame.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level4-jump.ini
stage level4-hold.ini
stage level4-x120.ini
stage level4-x200.ini
stage level4-x160.ini
stage level4-x128.ini
stage level4-x192.ini
stage level4-objs-start.ini
stage level2-frame.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage weapons-take.ini
stage level2-obj.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here (to 32), outside any hit, then
# clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b pc = $17
debug b pc = $18
debug b pc = $19
debug b pc = $1a
debug b pc = $1b
debug b pc = $1c
debug b pc = $1d
debug b pc = $1e
debug b pc = $1f
debug b pc = $20
debug b pc = $21
debug b pc = $22
debug b pc = $23
debug b pc = $24
debug b pc = $25
debug b pc = $26
debug b pc = $27
debug b pc = $28
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/level4-objs-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
